      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. it's a good start but it feels a little light for a formal regulatory summary. the regulators are really picky about seeing the specifics in the text rather than just high-level sentences. \n\ncould you expand this a bit? try to incorporate more of the specific metrics or breakdown the groups more clearly so the summary feels more \"data-heavy.\" like, if there are specific percentages or more granular numbers that support the efficacy and safety claims, make sure they are explicitly included in the prose. \n\nagain, just a reminder—tread carefully. i don't want you making up numbers or just throwing in random digits to boost that density score. it needs to be 100% accurate to the notes i gave you, just more detailed.",
