      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon review of the comprehensive findings from the Phase II clinical trial of AE-99, it has been observed that out of 295 participants divided equally across Group A and Group B, Group A, which comprised 148 patients, exhibited a significantly improved response rate when compared to Group B. Specifically, 120 patients in Group A received the immunotherapy, as opposed to Group B which derived 22% of its 145 patients into researchers. The efficacy was quantified, revealing a response improvement percentage of 15% for Group A versus a 2% control response rate seen in Group B, which translates to a robust 17% difference. Concerning safety, AE-99 demonstrated exceptional well-being among patients. Mild nausea was reported in 7% of the Group A subjects and 13% within Group B, maintaining the medication's tolerability. Throughout the trial, there were no life-threatening adverse events documented. The trial's achievement in meeting its primary endpoints corroborates the drug's potential for advancement towards widely accepted therapeutic applications, emphasizing AE-99's safety and responsiveness attributes. The trial's detailed metrics indicate a coherent and reliable conclusion that reinforces both the efficiency and tenability of AE-99 immunotherapy, with a notable 15% superiority in",
      "source": "target",
